# Local reference material.
#
# cuas/ holds C-UAS reference documents and notes kept on-disk for reading.
# Source material there is frequently vendor proprietary (marked company
# confidential, distribution-restricted, or similar), and this repository is
# public. Keep it untracked so it is never published by an ordinary commit.
#
# To version any of it, move it to a PRIVATE repository first.
cuas/

# Source documents generally: keep them out of the repo regardless of location.
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.key
